robe-encrypted-reasoning.mjs (manual injection, independent of\n173\t  this integration): same-account and cross-account replay of a real blob in\n174\t  a fabricated session is accepted across sessions, CLI versions, and a\n175\t  different paid ChatGPT account (identical token accounting), so the\n176\t  ciphertext is not keyed per-account; the free tier cannot run Codex at all.\n177\t  Still open: blob TTL, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves the same\n178\t  as ChatGPT auth — turnbridge attempts replay unconditionally either way\n179\t  since auth mode isn't observable from here; a rejected blob at actual\n180\t  `codex resume` time has no proactive detection and falls under the same\n181\t  `--bootstrap` escape hatch as any other fabrication-drift failure.\n182\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KKtySWjhQYMmEeaZbR7eEk","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"3505193d-c73d-4ab6-ad2e-acb0ca9c7915","promptId":"2af7b82c-699a-4944-8527-0ab917f7037e","sessionId":"a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3505193d-c73d-4ab6-ad2e-acb0ca9c7915","timestamp":"2026-07-27T06:48:47.377Z","toolUseResult":{"file":{"content":"# WIP technical design\n\n**Status:** MVP implemented for Claude Code ⇄ Codex; fabrication adapters are\nversion-pinned and must be revalidated per CLI release.\n\n## Main flow\n\n1. Conversation Ledger's hooks (`cledger install all`) capture each CLI's\n   local transcript incrementally into git notes as normalized\n   `conversation_turn` events, stamped with the repo's git identity\n   (`actor.id` = `user.email`) on human turns.\n2. `turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` lists conversations compatible with the\n   current repository state: events anchored to commits reachable from `HEAD`\n   (`--any-commit` lifts this), authored by you or unattributed\n   (`--all` includes collaborators).\n3. Selecting a conversation whose source matches the target CLI dele