{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"350\t\n351\tcasr's `project_dir_key` (all-non-alphanumeric → `-`) matches our directly\n352\tverified empirical result exactly — no divergence there.\n353\t\n354\t---\n355\t\n356\t## 7. Unknowns / risks\n357\t\n358\t- **Interactive (non-`-p`) resume was not tested** — this sandbox has no TUI.\n359\t  All verification used `claude --resume <id> -p \"<prompt>\" --max-turns 1`.\n360\t  It's possible interactive mode does additional validation (e.g. the casr\n361\t  \"hangs on load\" behavior) that print mode skips. Recommend a manual\n362\t  interactive smoke test (`claude --resume <id>` with no `-p`) before\n363\t  shipping turnbridge broadly.\n364\t- **Resume picker (`claude` / `/resume` with no ID) title source is\n365\t  inferred, not confirmed** — likely `ai-title` line content, falling back to\n366\t  first user message, but this is not independently verified against the\n367\t  actual interactive picker UI.\n368\t- **Timestamp format tolerance untested** — only millisecond-precision\n369\t  RFC3339 `...Z` strings were tried and confirmed required-present; unknown\n370\t  whether second-precision, offset-instead-of-Z, or out-of-order timestamps\n371\t  across lines are tolerated. Chronological, millisecond-precision,\n372\t  `Z`-suffixed timestamps are recommended to match real files exactly.\n373\t  Also unconfirmed whether timestamps must be internally consistent/ordered,\n374\t  or whether the file's own mtime vs. the JSON `timestamp` fields matter for\n375\t  session listing/sorting (e.g. in the resume picker's ordering).\n376\t  turnbridge should just use real, monotonically increasing timestamps to be\n377\t  safe.\n378\t- **Large/long sessions untested** — all fabricated test files were 2-3\n379\t  lines. Unknown if there's a line-count or byte-size behavior cliff, or\n380\t  whether very long fabricated histories affect context-loading correctly.\n381\t- **`sessionId` mismatch (inline field vs. filename) untested** — all our\n382\t  fabricated files either omitted the inline `sessionId` field or set it\n383\t  identically to the filename UUID. Behavior on mismatch is unknown;\n384\t  recommend always keeping them identical.\n385\t- **Duplicate/collided `uuid` values, or a `parentUuid` pointing to a\n386\t  nonexistent `uuid`, untested** — recommend generating fresh UUIDv4 per\n387\t  line and always chaining correctly (§2) to avoid undefined behavior.\n388\t- **`--resume` cwd-scoping workaround**: since resume is strictly scoped to\n389\t  the launch cwd's encoded project directory (§3), turnbridge must always\n390\t  `cd` (or set subprocess cwd) to match before invoking `claude --resume`.\n391\t  There is no `--project-dir`-style override flag observed in `claude\n392\t  --help` output for `--resume` specifically to bypass this.\n393\t- **Version string in fabricated lines**: casr uses the literal string\n394\t  `\"casr\"` as `version` and this apparently works for them; we recommend\n395\t  using a real, currently-installed version string (`\"2.1.215\"`) instead,\n396\t  purely for cosmetic consistency with real sessions — not confirmed to be\n397\t  functionally required either way (`version` was in the \"verified NOT","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KP4kZ6QLoTJ2p6KLVuNx17","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-spec-verification-gaps","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/spec-verification-gaps","head":"4751278e2d8945d1106edaf5990d13b3e1f330a8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","seq":49},"id":"ev1-a2bbca7d939a47b53852e75f7159548d426eea8aca97435da7b359dde827e4be","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T06:52:15.331Z","producer":{"session_id":"a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.11.0"},"raw":{"