{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"- What is this you say about, uh, token size estimates? Um, I don't like the idea that we're estimating token sizes. I assume we were working entirely in raw text given that, uh, token, like, token length is not transferable across models of different tokenizers.\n- not sur ei understand how we'ave got non-monotonic timestamps; Where are these time stamps coming from in the first place? Are they originally from Codex and Claude Code, and is your point that, like, when we record them, we may record them out of order? Is that what you're saying? Um, versus, like, trying to purposefully look through all the coding CLIs and all the time stamps on each thing and try and record them in order, I guess is your point?\n- Were we not already recording structured tool history? I thought we were. I assume Kledger does. Are you saying that Turnbridge does not currently transfer tool history? If so, that's odd to me. Um, but, also, maybe the problem here that I'm misunderstanding, um, do a lot of the agent de carnices currently run tools, get outputs, close tool, and, like, not actually keep all of the text in context? Is that what you're referring to? Like, is that introducing issues somewhere? I'm not quite sure with g six.\n- group B sounds easy enough to go ahead and do now\n1. cap. Please clarify for me as well the per model difference, like, what currently happens if I was using a one million context model, and I try and load it into a shorter, like, quarter million context model. I assume the existing Claude and Codex CLIs themselves have stuff against this that they won't actually run the model or they'll, like, trim to the most recent tokens or something. Um, just if you are aware, like, do we do anything in reference to context length, or do we just naively pass over context? I'm tempted to think that maybe we should be the ones just naively passing over the entire conversation and letting those tools handle if a combo is too long. Because I imagine they probably already have stuff for that, maybe not in terms of, like, maybe a given provider if they do not yet support a million context model, they only have five, twelve, or two fifty six or something, and they have my error. But I imagine a provider that supports up to a million context in some model probably can handle a a convo being transferred to a provider and to their smaller model because they probably already have built in, like, assertions and errors at that point. I don't know, though.\n2. I'm fine with a behavior change to shipped output because only I have used this so far and really only in testing and development. I have yet to actually, like, use it even myself in in, um, thoroughly, um, but I still... I'm not sure I understand the monotonicity issue.\n3. at least g seven through g nine sounded reasonable. If if you really think that g six count is just a feature, then I guess we could avoid it for now. Yeah.","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-spec-verification-gaps","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/spec-verification-gaps","head":"4751278e2d8945d1106edaf5990d13b3e1f330a8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","seq":109},"id":"ev1-b77ba1ecdbe29a32c90209db95d020738b5f859c4653b7f1b4914481d77ccbba","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T07:02:36.947Z","producer":{"session_id":"a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.11.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":"- What is this you say about, uh, token size estimates? Um, I don't like the idea that we're estimating token sizes. I assume we were working entirely in raw text given that, uh, 