{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"I read the roadmap in `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` (lines 122–181), checked `package.json`, and grepped `src/`, `scripts/`, and the docs for inline TODOs — there are none, so the roadmap is the only todo source.\n\n**Top 5, in the order the roadmap's own priorities imply:**\n\n1. **Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm, then swap the `file:` dep for a semver range.** This is the hard blocker on shipping turnbridge at all — `prepublishOnly` in `package.json:44` literally refuses to publish while the dep starts with `file:`. Deliberately deferred while both packages are dogfooded.\n\n2. **Adapter-drift automation stage 2.** `.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml` opens a tracking issue on drift today; the commented-out follow-on job would hand that issue to a Claude Code action to revalidate the spec and draft the PR. Needs an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repo secret and comfort with CI pushing branches.\n\n3. **Close the spec verification gaps.** Large/long histories (size cliffs, Codex auto-compaction), timestamp-format tolerance, sessionId/filename mismatch, duplicate or dangling uuid handling. Revalidation tooling already exists (`npm run smoke:interactive`, `scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs`) and is the stated bar for widening version pins.\n\n4. **Multi-hop reasoning carry-over.** Reasoning replay is gated per-event on `producer.source === \"codex\"`, which today equals a per-conversation check. Reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning via the `continuation` lineage chain when re-bridging was explicitly deferred as a follow-up.\n\n5. **Remaining encrypted-reasoning unknowns: blob TTL, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves like ChatGPT auth.** Turnbridge replays unconditionally since auth mode isn't observable from here; a blob rejected at real `codex resume` time has no proactive detection and falls back to `--bootstrap`.\n\nOne doc nit: the roadmap still tags encrypted-reasoning replay as *\"shipped, needs a turnbridge version bump\"* (line 143), but HEAD already bumped to 0.2.0 — that parenthetical is stale and can be dropped.\n\nresult: Top 5 turnbridge todos are (1) publish conversation-ledger to npm to unblock turnbridge's own publish, (2) adapter-drift automation stage 2, (3) close spec verification gaps on long histories/timestamps/uuids, (4) multi-hop reasoning carry-over via lineage, (5) resolve encrypted-reasoning blob TTL + API-org auth unknowns — plus a stale \"needs a version bump\" note at WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:143.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-spec-verification-gaps","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/.claude/worktrees/spec-verification-gaps","head":"4751278e2d8945d1106edaf5990d13b3e1f330a8","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","seq":30},"id":"ev1-1a52dc8584cdc4e614df300935136a01a5bdd084b611c9439d7e004aca0634f1","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-27T06:49:12.264Z","producer":{"session_id":"a6b0721f-3d36-4802-bc44-520ed792e1b6","source":"claude-code","tool":"cledger","version":"0.11.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"I read the roadmap in `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` (lines 122–181), checked `package.json`, and grepped `src/`, `scripts/`, and the docs for inline TODOs — there are none, so the roadmap is the only todo source.\n\n**Top 5, in the order the roadmap's own priorities imply:**\n\n1. **Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm, then swap the `file:` dep for a semver range.** This is the hard blocker on shipping turnbridge at all — `prepublishOnly` in `package.json:44` literally refuses to publish while the dep starts with `file:`. Deliberately deferred while both packages are dogfooded.\n\n2. **Adapter-drift automation stage 2.** `